# Published-page audit — orchestrator RESUME checkpoint

## WAVES 11–14 — A4 COMPLETE; WAVE 11 A6 IN PROGRESS (2026-08-10)

The owner directed the orchestrator to audit every remaining untagged page in
parallel and to continue autonomously from A0 through A10. Routine shell and
edit actions must never become permission prompts for the orchestrator or any
agent; an operation with no already-authorized form becomes a recorded blocker.
The shared baseline is clean `442f831c94882899c1dc5559b36599b0f78a99c8`,
which equals `origin/main`. Nothing has been published, committed, or pushed by
this run.

A0 was recomputed from current published pages, not from the prior list. The
scope is **14 pages / 7 A/B pairs / 223 unique untagged items / 188
proof-bearing items**: Wave 11 = 61/55, Wave 12 = 61/48, Wave 13 = 76/62,
Wave 14 = 25/23. All four category manifests are `real-analysis`, each contains
at most two pairs, and all four A0 suites pass 9/9. Relationship manifests are
exact and unresolved-free: Wave 11 = 790, Wave 12 = 890, Wave 13 = 487,
Wave 14 = 165.

All four GPT 5.6 Sol `xhigh`/1M Audit-Beta A1/A2 passes, all four independent
A3 receipts, and all four A4 applications are complete. The final A4 splits
are Wave 11 = 53 pure retags + 8 material items + one narrow page repair;
Wave 12 = 53 pure + 8 material; Wave 13 = 73 pure + 3 material; and Wave 14 =
20 pure + 5 material. Authoritative A4 gates are 13/13 for Waves 12–14. Wave
11 passes 12/13; its sole deliberate A6 hard edge is the generated-statement
contract for `fs-integration-by-parts-needs-no-integrability-hypothesis`, which
A3 explicitly reserved for Alpha disposition. Strict contracts otherwise pass:
55/55, 48/48, 62/62, and 23/23. Canonical `post-A4` snapshots and impact
